diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index 6853f0a..15faede 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -4,13 +4,15 @@
 - Bots are stored as `User` records with `role: :bot` (enum values: `member: 0, administrator: 1, bot: 2`).
 - `users.bot_token` stores a 24-character `SecureRandom.base58` credential (unique indexed, filtered from logs and `inspect` via `:token` in `filter_parameters`).
 - `users.creator_id` references the `User` who created the bot, enabling `User#can_administer?(bot)` for creators and administrators.
-- Reusing `User` gives bots room `Membership`s, automatic open room joining (`after_create_commit :grant_membership_to_open_rooms`), `Message` authorship (`creator_id`), `ActiveStorage` avatars, `@mention` support, and `Rooms::Closed` membership management out of the box.
-- Deleting a bot calls `User#deactivate`, which sets `status: :deactivated`, clears `bot_token: nil`, and removes non-direct memberships while preserving previously posted messages.
+- `users.add_to_all_open_rooms` (boolean, default `false`) controls whether a bot automatically joins open rooms. Unlike human users, bots no longer join `Rooms::Open` by default.
+- When `add_to_all_open_rooms` is enabled on create or update, `User::Bot#sync_open_room_memberships` grants membership to all existing `Rooms::Open` (skipping rooms the bot already belongs to). `Rooms::Open#grant_access_to_all_users` grants access to `User.open_room_members` (`User.active.without_bots` plus `User.bots.where(add_to_all_open_rooms: true)`). Disabling `add_to_all_open_rooms` preserves existing memberships.
+- Deleting a bot calls `User#deactivate`, which sets `status: :deactivated`, clears `bot_token: nil`, `webhook_url: nil`, `add_to_all_open_rooms: false`, and removes non-direct memberships while preserving previously posted messages.
 - Human-only flows (`SessionsController`, `Sessions::TransfersController`, `AccountsController`, `Accounts::UsersController`, `Users::SidebarsController`) scope with `User.without_bots`.
 
 ## UI Routes & Access Control
 - `/account/edit` exposes the "Set up chat bots" link (`/bots`) to all signed-in members.
 - `BotsController` (`/bots`, `/bots/new`, `/bots/:id/edit`) lists `Current.user.created_bots.active` for members and all `User.bots` for administrators on a single unpaginated page.
+- Bot forms (`app/views/bots/_form.html.erb`) expose `"Name the bot"`, optional `"Webhook URL"`, and the `"Add to all open rooms"` checkbox switch (off by default).
 - `edit`, `update`, and `destroy` require `Current.user.can_administer?(@bot)` (creator or administrator).
 
 ## HTTP Message API
@@ -21,8 +23,9 @@
 
 ## Outgoing Webhooks & Synchronous/Async Replies
 - `users.webhook_url` (optional string) is normalized (`strip.presence`), validated as an `http`/`https` URL when present, and cleared alongside `bot_token` on `User#deactivate`.
-- Bot forms (`app/views/bots/_form.html.erb`) expose the optional `"Webhook URL"` input; submitting an empty value clears `webhook_url`.
 - `Message::Mentionee#mentioned_bots` selects active bots that are members of the room (excluding `message.creator`) referenced in ActionText mention attachments.
-- `Room#receive(message)` enqueues `User::Bot::WebhookJob` per mentioned bot with a `webhook_url`, so webhook HTTP delivery never blocks the message creator's request.
-- `User::Bot::Webhook` POSTs `Content-Type: application/json` (`event: "mention"`, `author`, `room` with `reply_to` path `/rooms/:room_id/:bot_token/messages`, `message` with `body.text` stripped of that bot's own `@`-mention attachment, `body.html`, and `link` `/rooms/:room_id/@:message_id`).
+- `Room#receive(message)` enqueues `User::Bot::WebhookJob` (`event: "mention"`) per mentioned bot with a `webhook_url`.
+- Whenever a bot with a `webhook_url` is newly added to a non-direct room (`Rooms::Open` or `Rooms::Closed`)—whether via `Room#memberships.grant_to`, `Membership.create!`, `Rooms::Open` creation/conversion, or `add_to_all_open_rooms`—`Room#deliver_joined_webhooks_later` / `User::Bot#deliver_joined_webhook_later` enqueues `User::Bot::WebhookJob` (`event: "joined"`) once per newly added `(bot, room)` pair. `Rooms::Direct` never triggers `joined`.
+- `User::Bot::WebhookJob` uses `enqueue_after_transaction_commit = true` so workers only run after memberships and rooms are committed.
+- `User::Bot::Webhook` POSTs `Content-Type: application/json` for `mention` (`event`, `author`, `room`, `message`) and `joined` (`event: "joined"`, `room: { id, name, reply_to }`).
 - Synchronous `200` responses with `Content-Type: text/plain` (HTML-escaped with `<br>` newlines) or `text/html` create and broadcast a reply message from the bot; `204` or non-matching responses post nothing.
